= The Healthcare Rollout

The Affordable Care Act's coverage provisions have taken effect, but the rollout has been rocky: website failures, cancelled plans, and a flood of attack ads. Millions are nonetheless enrolling.

How should the party respond?

- @aca_defend: Defend the law loudly
- @aca_fix: Focus on fixing the problems
- @aca_distance: Keep our distance

@aca_defend
on-arrival: uninsured -= 1; progressive_dissent -= 2; moderate_dissent += 2; dem_enthusiasm += 0.3; gop_enthusiasm += 0.3

We run a loud, proud campaign on healthcare. Enrollment surges; so do the attacks.

@aca_fix
on-arrival: uninsured -= 1.5; moderate_strength += 2; suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent += 2

We concede mistakes, fix the website, and extend enrollment deadlines. Coverage numbers improve.

@aca_distance
on-arrival: moderate_dissent -= 2; progressive_dissent += 4; working_dem -= 2*(1-dissent)

Vulnerable candidates avoid mentioning the law. Our base notices.
